course: dictionary
lesson: 11720
title: Who Says Yes?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To authorise something means to give official permission for it to happen. The person in charge says yes, and then it is allowed. «The head teacher authorised a day off for the school trip.» The head is in charge, so the day off is now official.
explain: Authorise can also mean to give someone the power or right to do something. «Only the bank manager can authorise a payment.» This tells you that only one person has the right to say yes.
explain: Look for clue words around it, such as official, power, right, or in charge. «An unauthorised absence» means a day away from school that nobody approved. The prefix un- means not, so unauthorised means not approved.
fact: Authorise is a verb: authorise, authorises, authorised, authorising.
fact: «Authorise» means to give official permission for something to happen.
fact: «Authorise» can also mean to give someone the power or right to do something.
fact: In American English, the spelling is authorize.
fact: The prefix «un-» means not, so «unauthorised» means not given permission.
exercise: «Only the manager can authorise a payment.» What does authorise mean here? | Say no to | Lose track of | *Give official permission for | Count up
exercise: «An unauthorised absence is a day away that nobody approved.» What does un- tell you? | *It means not | It means before | It means very large | It means again
exercise: Yesterday the head ___ the trip. Which word fits? | authorising | authorise | *authorised | authorises
test: «The council authorised the new park.» What does authorised mean? | Painted it in bright colours | Built a fence around it | Stopped it being used | *Officially approved it
test: Which is the US spelling of authorise? | authorise | authoriz | authorice | *authorize
exam: «Only an authorised person can sign the form.» What is an authorised person? | A person who forgets things | A person who is very tall | A person who wants to go home | *A person given the right to approve it
